            <ArticleTitle>Inferior vena cava filter penetration into right proximal ureter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>7160-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Inferior vena cava (IVC) filter penetration into the renal collecting system is an infrequent event. We report a case of IVC filter penetration into the right proximal ureter resulting in gross hematuria, hydronephrosis and stone formation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
